	<div class="widgetBody pageStyles" id="div6fff3f01-8ae7-43db-b456-b8534afd633d">

		<div style="min-height: 18px;">
			<div class="textContent" ><h2 style="text-align: center;"><span style="font-size: 1.4em;"><br></span></h2><h2 style="text-align: center;"><strong style="font-size: 0.99em;">2026 Elections</strong></h2><h2 style="text-align: center;"><br></h2><h2 style="text-align: center;">General Election - November 3, 2026</h2><div style="text-align: center;"><strong><em>Governor</em></strong></div><div style="text-align: center;"><strong><em><br></em></strong></div><div style="text-align: center;"><strong><em>Lieutenant Governor</em></strong></div><div style="text-align: center;"><strong><em><br></em></strong></div><div style="text-align: center;"><strong><em>Attorney General</em></strong></div><div style="text-align: center;"><strong><em><br></em></strong></div><div style="text-align: center;"><strong><em>Secretary of State</em></strong></div><div style="text-align: center;"><strong><em><br></em></strong></div><div style="text-align: center;"><strong><em>State Treasurer</em></strong></div><div style="text-align: center;"><strong><em><br></em></strong></div><div style="text-align: center;"><strong><em>Representative in Congress District 4</em></strong></div><div style="text-align: center;"><strong><em><br></em></strong></div><div style="text-align: center;"><strong><em>Representative to the Assembly District 23</em></strong></div><div style="text-align: center;"><strong><em><br></em></strong></div><div style="text-align: center;"><strong><em>Milwaukee County Sheriff</em></strong></div><div style="text-align: center;"><strong><em><br></em></strong></div><div style="text-align: center;"><strong><em>Milwaukee County Clerk of Circuit Court</em></strong></div><h2 style="text-align: center;"><br></h2><h2 style="text-align: center;"><span style="font-family: &quot;Open Sans&quot;; font-size: 0.99em; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400; text-align: center; color: rgb(56, 56, 56);">- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -</span></h2><p style="text-align: center;">Polling places are open for all Elections from 7:00 am - 8:00 pm on Election Day.</p><p style="text-align: center;" class="">Please use the <a href="https://www.wfbvillage.gov/DocumentCenter/View/508/Ward-map" class="docaccess-activated" data-docaccess-source-url="https://www.wfbvillage.gov/DocumentCenter/View/508/Ward-map" data-url-hash="606e12644bbb0ba2eddd9da97df996d474b81fe31e4b8fc725e1d7ef66f841fd" data-url-status="disabled"></a><a href="https://www.wfbvillage.gov/DocumentCenter/View/3014/Voting-Location-Map-" class="docaccess-activated" data-docaccess-source-url="https://www.wfbvillage.gov/DocumentCenter/View/3014/Voting-Location-Map-" data-url-hash="46ecfd8af694dd68e72af79a8f4b7a4132b3a75a0c5ed4882211fe5aa915e453" data-url-status="disabled">Ward Map</a> (PDF) or <a href="https://myvote.wi.gov/en-us/">MyVote.wi.gov</a> to see where your polling place is.</p><p style="text-align: center;">- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -</p><p style="text-align: center;"><strong>Election Day Registration</strong></p><p style="text-align: center;" class="">Voters who need to register on Election Day should go to their polling place (<a href="https://www.wfbvillage.gov/DocumentCenter/View/508/Ward-map" class="docaccess-activated" data-docaccess-source-url="https://www.wfbvillage.gov/DocumentCenter/View/508/Ward-map" data-url-hash="606e12644bbb0ba2eddd9da97df996d474b81fe31e4b8fc725e1d7ef66f841fd" data-url-status="disabled"></a><a href="https://www.wfbvillage.gov/DocumentCenter/View/3014/Voting-Location-Map-" class="docaccess-activated" data-docaccess-source-url="https://www.wfbvillage.gov/DocumentCenter/View/3014/Voting-Location-Map-" data-url-hash="46ecfd8af694dd68e72af79a8f4b7a4132b3a75a0c5ed4882211fe5aa915e453" data-url-status="disabled">find your polling location</a>).</p><p style="text-align: center;">Voters must be 18 years or older, a US Citizen and reside at their current residence for 28 consecutive days immediately proceeding the Election to be eligible elector.</p><p style="text-align: center;">Proof of residence is required for all registrations.</p><p style="text-align: center;">Registration will be completed on Badger Books therefore no paper form is required.</p><p style="text-align: center;">- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -</p><p style="text-align: center;"><strong>&nbsp;Sample Ballot</strong></p><p style="text-align: center;"><em class="startContainer endContainer"><a href="https://www.wfbvillage.gov/DocumentCenter/View/3384/Whitefish-Bay-Sample-11032026">Sample Ballot - November 3, 2026</a></em></p><p style="text-align: center;">****Ballots for all Whitefish Bay wards are the same.***</p><p style="text-align: center;">- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -</p><p style="text-align: center;">****Wisconsin Requires a Photo ID to Vote****</p><p style="text-align: center;">For more information about the voter identification law, visit the State of Wisconsin site.</p><p style="text-align: center;"><a href="https://elections.wi.gov/sites/default/files/documents/Photo%20ID%20%26%20Voting%20Guide.pdf" class="docaccess-activated" data-docaccess-source-url="https://elections.wi.gov/sites/default/files/documents/Photo%20ID%20%26%20Voting%20Guide.pdf" data-url-hash="481a85bc9e631638458ef64427ca5f8357411d4aa8ac9aef23a0c085a233c80b" data-url-status="disabled">Wisconsin Election Commission Photo ID &amp; Voting Guide</a></p><p style="text-align: center;">- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -</p><p style="text-align: center;"><strong>Ward Map</strong></p><p style="text-align: center;" class="">Please use the <a href="https://www.wfbvillage.gov/DocumentCenter/View/3014/Voting-Location-Map-" class="docaccess-activated" data-docaccess-source-url="https://www.wfbvillage.gov/DocumentCenter/View/3014/Voting-Location-Map-" data-url-hash="46ecfd8af694dd68e72af79a8f4b7a4132b3a75a0c5ed4882211fe5aa915e453" data-url-status="disabled">Ward Map</a> (PDF) or <a href="https://myvote.wi.gov/en-us/">MyVote.wi.gov</a> to see where your polling place is. Polling places are open from 7:00am - 8:00pm on Election Day.</p><p style="text-align: center;">- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -</p><p><strong>Voting Questions</strong></p><p class="">For voting questions or to request an absentee ballot, send an email to <a href="mailto: elections@whitefishbaywi.gov">elections@whitefishbaywi.gov</a>, contact the Village Clerk’s office at 414-962-6690, or visit the <a href="https://elections.wi.gov/">Wisconsin Elections Commission website</a>.</p></div>
		</div>
	</div>
</div>

<style>
	.widget .textContent p:first-child {
		padding-top: 0px;
		margin-top: 0px;
	}

</style>


				</div>
					<ol class="tabbedWidgetNarrow cpTabs  accordion"  aria-hidden="False.ToString().ToLowerInvariant()" >
						<li class="" role="presentation">	<a href="#tab37d34a21-5fbf-43cc-9f0b-0e4aa4334694_1" class="tabButton" id="tabBtnNarrow37d34a21-5fbf-43cc-9f0b-0e4aa4334694_1" role="button" aria-controls="tab37d34a21-5fbf-43cc-9f0b-0e4aa4334694_1" aria-expanded="false" ><span class="tabName editable" data-sequence="1" data-tabname="Registration" contenteditable="false">Registration</span></a>
</li>
					</ol>
				<div class="tabbedWidget cpTabPanel " style="display: none;" id="tab37d34a21-5fbf-43cc-9f0b-0e4aa4334694_1" role="region" aria-labelledby="tabBtn37d34a21-5fbf-43cc-9f0b-0e4aa4334694_1" >




<div data-widget-id="3192e6c9-5cf6-4ac9-ac7a-25750718b101" data-moduleName="list" id="widgetText3192e6c9-5cf6-4ac9-ac7a-25750718b101" class="widget widgetText">
	<div class="widgetBody pageStyles" id="div3192e6c9-5cf6-4ac9-ac7a-25750718b101">

		<div style="min-height: 18px;">
			<div class="textContent" ><p style="text-align: center;"><strong>Voter Registration</strong></p><p style="text-align: center;">New voters, voters who have moved or had a name change are required to register. Registration can be completed in one of the following ways:</p><p style="text-align: center;">Online at: <a href="https://myvote.wi.gov/en-us/">https://myvote.wi.gov/en-us/</a></p><p class="" style="text-align: center;">Complete a <a href="https://www.wfbvillage.gov/DocumentCenter/View/243/Wisconsin-Voter-Registration-Application-PDF" class="docaccess-activated" data-docaccess-source-url="https://www.wfbvillage.gov/DocumentCenter/View/243/Wisconsin-Voter-Registration-Application-PDF" data-url-hash="b84103756afd74d410b48e2ae24eb075e56b7f0a27f6db7433d3c3029acb84a7" data-url-status="disabled"></a><a href="https://elections.wi.gov/sites/default/files/legacy/2020-06/El-131%2520Voter%2520Registration%2520App_Fillable-%2520%2528REV%25202020-06%2529_0.pdf" class="docaccess-activated" data-docaccess-source-url="https://elections.wi.gov/sites/default/files/legacy/2020-06/El-131%2520Voter%2520Registration%2520App_Fillable-%2520%2528REV%25202020-06%2529_0.pdf" data-url-hash="b84103756afd74d410b48e2ae24eb075e56b7f0a27f6db7433d3c3029acb84a7" data-url-status="disabled">Wisconsin Voter Registration Application form  (EL-131)</a>.</p><p style="text-align: center;"><em>Voters must be 18 years or older, a US Citizen and reside at their current residence for 28 consecutive days immediately proceeding the Election to be eligible elector.</em></p><p style="text-align: center;"><em class="">Proof of residence is required for all registrations. <a href="https://elections.wi.gov/sites/default/files/documents/Photo%20ID%20%26%20Voting%20Guide.pdf" class="docaccess-activated" data-docaccess-source-url="https://elections.wi.gov/sites/default/files/documents/Photo%20ID%20%26%20Voting%20Guide.pdf" data-url-hash="481a85bc9e631638458ef64427ca5f8357411d4aa8ac9aef23a0c085a233c80b" data-url-status="disabled">Wisconsin Election Commission Photo ID &amp; Voting Guide</a></em></p><p style="text-align: center;">Applications can be accepted by online or mail through the 20th day prior to an Election</p><p style="text-align: center;">Within 20 days of an Election applications are required to be submitted in person at the Municipal Clerk's Office through the Friday prior to the Election.</p><p style="text-align: center;">There is no registering on the Monday before any Election.</p><p style="text-align: center;"><br></p><p style="text-align: center;"><strong>&nbsp;Election Day Registration&nbsp;</strong></p><p style="text-align: center;" class="">Voters who need to register on Election Day should go to their polling place (<a href="https://www.wfbvillage.gov/DocumentCenter/View/3014/Voting-Location-Map-" class="docaccess-activated" data-docaccess-source-url="https://www.wfbvillage.gov/DocumentCenter/View/3014/Voting-Location-Map-" data-url-hash="46ecfd8af694dd68e72af79a8f4b7a4132b3a75a0c5ed4882211fe5aa915e453" data-url-status="disabled">find your polling location</a>).</p><p style="text-align: center;">Voters must be 18 years or older, a US Citizen and reside at their current residence for 28 consecutive days immediately proceeding the Election to be eligible elector.</p><p class="" style="text-align: center;"><a href="https://elections.wi.gov/sites/default/files/documents/Photo%20ID%20%26%20Voting%20Guide.pdf" class="docaccess-activated startContainer" data-docaccess-source-url="https://www.wfbvillage.gov/DocumentCenter/View/2201/November-5-2024-Sample-Ballot" data-url-hash="47f9e8878c0343b580e0c435784d0cb2c49a7ecae0847014d0615e3ef20f7034" data-url-status="disabled">Proof of residence is required for all registrations. </a><a href="https://elections.wi.gov/sites/default/files/documents/Photo%20ID%20%26%20Voting%20Guide.pdf" class="docaccess-activated endContainer" data-docaccess-source-url="https://elections.wi.gov/sites/default/files/documents/Photo%20ID%20%26%20Voting%20Guide.pdf" data-url-hash="481a85bc9e631638458ef64427ca5f8357411d4aa8ac9aef23a0c085a233c80b" data-url-status="disabled">Wisconsin Election Commission Photo ID &amp; Voting Guide</a></p><p style="text-align: center;">Registration will be completed on Badger Books therefore no paper form is required.</p><p style="text-align: center;"><br></p><p style="text-align: center;"><strong>Voting Questions</strong></p><p class="" style="text-align: center;">For voting questions or to request an absentee ballot, send an email to <a href="mailto: elections@whitefishbaywi.gov">elections@whitefishbaywi.gov</a>, contact the Village Clerk’s office at 414-962-6690, or visit the <a href="https://elections.wi.gov/photoid" class=""></a><a href="https://elections.wi.gov/">Wisconsin Elections Commission website</a>.</p><p><br></p></div>
		</div>
	</div>
</div>

<style>
	.widget .textContent p:first-child {
		padding-top: 0px;
		margin-top: 0px;
	}

</style>


				</div>
					<ol class="tabbedWidgetNarrow cpTabs  accordion"  aria-hidden="False.ToString().ToLowerInvariant()" >
						<li class="" role="presentation">	<a href="#tab37d34a21-5fbf-43cc-9f0b-0e4aa4334694_2" class="tabButton" id="tabBtnNarrow37d34a21-5fbf-43cc-9f0b-0e4aa4334694_2" role="button" aria-controls="tab37d34a21-5fbf-43cc-9f0b-0e4aa4334694_2" aria-expanded="false" ><span class="tabName editable" data-sequence="2" data-tabname="Mailed Absentee Ballots" contenteditable="false">Mailed Absentee Ballots</span></a>
</li>
					</ol>
				<div class="tabbedWidget cpTabPanel " style="display: none;" id="tab37d34a21-5fbf-43cc-9f0b-0e4aa4334694_2" role="region" aria-labelledby="tabBtn37d34a21-5fbf-43cc-9f0b-0e4aa4334694_2" >




<div data-widget-id="46a9a55b-281e-4979-8171-91a6c07f6a7e" data-moduleName="list" id="widgetText46a9a55b-281e-4979-8171-91a6c07f6a7e" class="widget widgetText">
	<div class="widgetBody pageStyles" id="div46a9a55b-281e-4979-8171-91a6c07f6a7e">

		<div style="min-height: 18px;">
			<div class="textContent" ><p style="text-align: center;"><strong>Absentee Ballot Requests</strong></p><p style="text-align: center;">Voting by mail is easy and secure. Absentee ballots can be requested in one of the following ways:</p><p style="text-align: center;"><strong>Online</strong> at: <a href="https://myvote.wi.gov/en-us/">https://myvote.wi.gov/en-us/</a> (preferred method)</p><p style="text-align: center;">Send a request via <strong>email</strong> to elections@whitefishbaywi.gov (please include a copy of WI photo ID)</p><p style="text-align: center;" class="">Submit an Absentee Ballot Application by <strong>mail</strong>. Application is available online at: <a href="https://www.wfbvillage.gov/DocumentCenter/View/2375/Absentee-Ballot-Request---EL-121">Absentee Ballot Request (EL-121)</a></p><p style="text-align: center;">Voters who have not previously submitted a copy of their photo ID to vote by mail will need to include a copy of their ID with their request. If you are not sure whether you need to do so, please include a copy to avoid any delay in processing.</p><p style="text-align: center;" class=""><a href="https://www.wfbvillage.gov/DocumentCenter/View/508/Ward-map" class="docaccess-activated" data-docaccess-source-url="https://www.wfbvillage.gov/DocumentCenter/View/508/Ward-map" data-url-hash="606e12644bbb0ba2eddd9da97df996d474b81fe31e4b8fc725e1d7ef66f841fd" data-url-status="disabled"></a><a href="https://www.wfbvillage.gov/DocumentCenter/View/508/Ward-map" class="docaccess-activated" data-docaccess-source-url="https://www.wfbvillage.gov/DocumentCenter/View/508/Ward-map" data-url-hash="606e12644bbb0ba2eddd9da97df996d474b81fe31e4b8fc725e1d7ef66f841fd" data-url-status="disabled"></a><strong>Track Absentee Ballot online:</strong> Click <a href="https://www.wfbvillage.gov/DocumentCenter/View/1701/Tracking-your-absentee-ballot---MyVote" class="docaccess-activated" data-docaccess-source-url="https://www.wfbvillage.gov/DocumentCenter/View/1701/Tracking-your-absentee-ballot---MyVote" data-url-hash="d42a81eaec6e557dfa89738c3c340a3e126316f05a0b43df62ad48f7448432e8" data-url-status="disabled">HERE</a> to see instructions on how to track your absentee ballot.</p><p style="text-align: center;">- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -</p><p style="text-align: center;">&nbsp;<strong>Sample Ballot</strong></p><p style="text-align: center;"><span style="font-size: 15.6816px;" class="startContainer endContainer"><a href="https://www.wfbvillage.gov/DocumentCenter/View/3384/Whitefish-Bay-Sample-11032026">Sample Ballot - November 3, 2026</a></span></p><p style="text-align: center;"><span style="font-family: &quot;Open Sans&quot;; font-size: 0.99em; font-style: normal; font-weight: 400;">****Ballots for all Whitefish Bay wards are the same.***</span></p><p style="text-align: center;">- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -</p><p style="text-align: center;">****Wisconsin Requires a Photo ID to Vote****</p><p style="text-align: center;">For more information about the voter identification law, visit the State of Wisconsin site. <a href="https://elections.wi.gov/sites/default/files/documents/Photo%20ID%20%26%20Voting%20Guide.pdf" class="docaccess-activated" data-docaccess-source-url="https://elections.wi.gov/sites/default/files/documents/Photo%20ID%20%26%20Voting%20Guide.pdf" data-url-hash="481a85bc9e631638458ef64427ca5f8357411d4aa8ac9aef23a0c085a233c80b" data-url-status="disabled">Wisconsin Election Commission Photo ID &amp; Voting Guide&nbsp;</a></p><p style="text-align: center;">- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -</p><h3 style="text-align: center;"><strong>&nbsp;Returning An Absentee Ballot</strong></h3><p style="text-align: center;"><span style="font-weight: normal; text-align: center;">Absentee Ballots may be returned to the Village Clerk's in one of the following ways:</span></p><p style="text-align: center;"><span style="font-weight: normal; text-align: center;">1. </span><span style="text-align: center;"><strong>Mail </strong></span><span style="font-weight: normal; text-align: center;">Absentee Ballot with USPS (postage is provided)</span></p><p style="text-align: center;"><span style="font-weight: normal; text-align: center;">2. </span><span style="text-align: center;"><strong>Drop off in person</strong></span><span style="font-weight: normal; text-align: center;"> at the Administration Counter at Village Hall</span></p><p style="text-align: center;"><span style="font-weight: normal; text-align: center;">3. </span><span style="text-align: center;"><strong>Use the drop box</strong></span><span style="font-weight: normal; text-align: center;"> located between the front doors at Village Hall labeled for Ballots</span></p><p style="text-align: center;"><span style="font-weight: normal; text-align: center;"><br></span></p><p style="text-align: center;"><span style="font-weight: normal; text-align: center;"><em>Per WI Court Ruling each voter is required to return their own ballot unless the voter self-identifies as being disabled and appoints someone to submit the ballot for them.</em></span></p><p style="text-align: center;"><span style="text-align: center;" class=""><strong>Track Your Ballot Online: </strong>Voter may track their ballot on <a href="https://myvote.wi.gov/en-us/">MyVote.wi.gov</a>&nbsp;</span></p><p style="text-align: center;"><span style="text-align: center;" class="">Click <a href="https://myvote.wi.gov/en-us/">HERE</a> for instruction on how to Track Your Ballot.</span></p><p><strong><br></strong></p><p><strong>Voting Questions</strong></p><p class="">For voting questions or to request an absentee ballot, send an email to <a href="mailto: elections@whitefishbaywi.gov">elections@whitefishbaywi.gov</a>, contact the Village Clerk’s office at 414-962-6690, or visit the <a href="https://elections.wi.gov/">Wisconsin Elections Commission website</a>.</p><p><br></p><p><br></p><p><br></p></div>
		</div>
	</div>
</div>

<style>
	.widget .textContent p:first-child {
		padding-top: 0px;
		margin-top: 0px;
	}

</style>


				</div>
					<ol class="tabbedWidgetNarrow cpTabs  accordion"  aria-hidden="False.ToString().ToLowerInvariant()" >
						<li class="" role="presentation">	<a href="#tab37d34a21-5fbf-43cc-9f0b-0e4aa4334694_3" class="tabButton" id="tabBtnNarrow37d34a21-5fbf-43cc-9f0b-0e4aa4334694_3" role="button" aria-controls="tab37d34a21-5fbf-43cc-9f0b-0e4aa4334694_3" aria-expanded="false" ><span class="tabName editable" data-sequence="3" data-tabname="In-Person Absentee Voting" contenteditable="false">In-Person Absentee Voting</span></a>
</li>
					</ol>
				<div class="tabbedWidget cpTabPanel " style="display: none;" id="tab37d34a21-5fbf-43cc-9f0b-0e4aa4334694_3" role="region" aria-labelledby="tabBtn37d34a21-5fbf-43cc-9f0b-0e4aa4334694_3" >




<div data-widget-id="c2f0e2d4-f3f9-49e9-abd1-8fd362ca7d24" data-moduleName="list" id="widgetTextc2f0e2d4-f3f9-49e9-abd1-8fd362ca7d24" class="widget widgetText">
	<div class="widgetBody pageStyles" id="divc2f0e2d4-f3f9-49e9-abd1-8fd362ca7d24">

		<div style="min-height: 18px;">
			<div class="textContent" ><p>In- Person Absentee Voting for all wards occurs at Village Hall (5300 N Marlborough Drive) starting the Tuesday 2 weeks prior to an Election through the Friday immediately preceding the Election, Monday through Friday 8:00 am to 4:30 pm (open until 5:00 pm on the Thursday and Friday immediately preceding an Election).</p><p style="text-align: center;">- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -</p><p style="text-align: center;">&nbsp;<strong>Sample Ballot</strong></p><p class="startContainer endContainer" style="text-align: center;"><a href="https://www.wfbvillage.gov/DocumentCenter/View/3384/Whitefish-Bay-Sample-11032026">Sample Ballot&nbsp;- November 3, 2026</a></p><p style="text-align: center;">****Ballots for all Whitefish Bay wards are the same.***</p><p style="text-align: center;">- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -</p><p style="text-align: center;"><strong>****Wisconsin Requires a Photo ID to Vote****</strong></p><p style="text-align: center;">For more information about the voter identification law, visit the State of Wisconsin site. <a href="https://elections.wi.gov/sites/default/files/documents/Photo%20ID%20%26%20Voting%20Guide.pdf" class="docaccess-activated" data-docaccess-source-url="https://elections.wi.gov/sites/default/files/documents/Photo%20ID%20%26%20Voting%20Guide.pdf" data-url-hash="481a85bc9e631638458ef64427ca5f8357411d4aa8ac9aef23a0c085a233c80b" data-url-status="disabled"></a>Wisconsin Election Commission Photo ID &amp; Voting Guide</p><p style="text-align: center;"><br></p><p><strong>Voting Questions</strong></p><p class="">For voting questions or to request an absentee ballot, send an email to <a href="mailto: elections@whitefishbaywi.gov">elections@whitefishwi.gov</a>, contact the Village Clerk’s office at 414-962-6690, or visit the <a href="https://elections.wi.gov/">Wisconsin Elections Commission website</a>.</p></div>
		</div>
	</div>
</div>

<style>
	.widget .textContent p:first-child {
		padding-top: 0px;
		margin-top: 0px;
	}

</style>


				</div>
					<ol class="tabbedWidgetNarrow cpTabs  accordion"  aria-hidden="False.ToString().ToLowerInvariant()" >
